      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): prove post-action target continuity before adopting a tab",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nAfter a browser navigation or action invalidates the selected raw target, route code retried tab lists and adopted replacements via heuristics: any sole remaining tab, a uniquely new post-action tab, or a uniquely URL-matching tab. None of those prove the acted-on page identity, so `/act` could return an unrelated tab's `targetId` and silently redirect the caller's next mutating action onto the wrong page.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nClawSweeper's recommended path: make each backend return its operation-owned target outcome; remove route-level list inference entirely. Playwright navigate/act now read the acted-on page's raw target id via `Target.getTargetInfo` after the operation and return it on the result. Routes apply `resolveOperationTargetOutcome`: backend-reported id when present, otherwise the acted-on id (stale/closed) so callers require a fresh selection.\n\nRemoved heuristics:\n- adopting a uniquely new post-action tab\n- adopting a uniquely URL-matching tab (renderer swap inferred from lists)\n\nExtension-relay profiles use Playwright `readPageTargetId` for navigate/act outcomes. The relay bridge now exposes a stable public handle `openclaw-relay-tab-{tabId}` that survives chrome.debugger renderer detach/reattach; CDP clients see the public id while the bridge tracks raw attachment ids internally. Chrome MCP existing-session uses tab-list membership via `readChromeMcpOperationTargetId` after navigate/act; close reports `operationTargetId: null`.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- **Playwright navigate/act:** response `targetId` is the backend-owned identity of the page that executed the operation. If the page closes, the acted-on id is returned (stale) and callers must re-select.\n- **Extension-relay /navigate:** route applies `resolveOperationTargetOutcome` to `readPageTargetId` / `navigateViaPlaywright` outcomes (no list inference). Relay CDP clients see stable `openclaw-relay-tab-{tabId}` handles across renderer swaps.\n- **Chrome MCP existing-session /act:** route applies `resolveOperationTargetOutcome` to tab-list membership; stale acted-on id preserved when the tab is gone.\n- **No wrong-tab routing:** unrelated tabs left open are never adopted from tab lists, URL cardinality, or sole-tab fallback.\n- **Continuity preserved:** renderer swaps and action-triggered replacements still work when the backend reports the new raw target id (#25323 / #25326 / #46137).\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Live browser proof (real Chrome/CDP, route-level contracts)\n\nHarness: `extensions/browser/scripts/proof-103785-target-continuity.test-harness.mts`\n\nRun:\n\n```\npnpm exec tsx extensions/browser/scripts/proof-103785-target-continuity.test-harness.mts\n```\n\nRedacted output:\n\n```\n=== Live-browser proof for #103785 (backend-owned page identity) ===\n\nScenario A: action closes acted-on tab A; unrelated tab B survives\n  kept acted-on identity A: true\n  adopted unrelated survivor B: false\n  PASS: unrelated survivor B was NOT adopted.\n\nScenario B: renderer swap (page reattaches under new raw target at navigated url)\n  adopted backend-reported reattached target: true\n  PASS: renderer-swap continuity preserved.\n\nScenario C: extension-relay /navigate route (readPageTargetId post-navigate + route resolver)\n  readPageTargetId (navigateViaPlaywright return contract)=BCC5F455… url=http://[redacted-host]/…\n  /navigate route outcome target=BCC5F455… (acted-on=BCC5F455…)\n  adopted backend-reported post-navigate target: true\n  PASS: extension-relay route preserved backend-owned identity.\n\nScenario D: Chrome MCP existing-session /act route (tab-list membership + resolver)\n  D1 tab still in list: kept acted-on identity when tab survives: true\n  D2 tab gone after close: stale acted-on id preserved when tab is gone: true\n  PASS: Chrome MCP route contract honored for survive + close.\n\nScenario E: paired extension-relay (connectOverCDP + detach/reattach + navigate + act)\n  E2 connectOverCDP createTarget public handle=openclaw…\n  E2 readPageTargetId=[fallback] /navigate backend=openclaw… route=openclaw… url=[redacted]\n  route continuity on stable public handle: true\n  E1 bridge CDP detach/reattach public handle=openclaw… stable=true\n  E1 subsequent Runtime.evaluate on reattached session: true\n  PASS: paired extension-relay detach/reattach + navigate + act.\n\n=== ALL SCENARIOS PASSED ===\n```\n\nScenario E uses a scripted loopback relay server plus `connectOverCDP` to the relay CDP endpoint. It covers: renderer detach → reattach on the stable public handle → successful follow-up `Runtime.evaluate` on the same tab session, plus route-level continuity via `resolveOperationTargetOutcome` on the stable public id. This is redacted paired-relay proof without a live Chrome extension install; production extension pairing would exercise the same bridge contract end-to-end.\n\n### Relay-bridge regression (stable public handle)\n\n`relay-bridge.test.ts` includes: **preserves relay-owned public target id across renderer detach and reattach**. Public id format: `openclaw-relay-tab-{tabId}`. `Target.getTargetInfo` and attach/detach events surface the public id; raw chrome.debugger ids stay internal.\n\n### Maintainer decision: relay-stable public handle\n\n**Implemented (Option 1):** stable relay public handles in `relay-bridge.ts`. Recommend `@steipete` confirm this matches the intended relay public identity contract, or whether production should retain temporary recovery until migration.\n\n### Source and test changes\n\n- `resolveOperationTargetOutcome` replaces list-inference resolver; no tab-list adoption.\n- `readPageTargetId` exported from Playwright session; `navigateViaPlaywright` and `executeActViaPlaywright` return `targetId`.\n- `readChromeMcpOperationTargetId` exported; Chrome MCP existing-session `/act` and close wire operation-owned outcomes.\n- Extension-relay `/navigate` and Playwright `/act` paths wire backend outcomes via `resolveOperationTargetOutcome`.\n- `relay-bridge.ts`: stable public target ids across detach/reattach; bridge regression test added.\n- Proof harness Scenario E: paired-relay detach/reattach + act over connectOverCDP.\n- Tests updated; contract test for #46137 mocks backend `targetId` on act result; Chrome MCP membership regressions added.\n\nAutomated tests:\n\n```\npnpm test:extension browser -- extensions/browser/src/browser/extension-relay/relay-bridge.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/agent.snapshot.test.ts\n# relay-bridge 13 passed | agent.snapshot 8 passed\n```\n\nExtension package boundary typecheck: `extension package boundary check passed`.\n\nCloses #103785\n",
